  "steps": [
    "Add the beans, 12 cups of water and the charro bean seasoning to a slow cooker and cook.",
    "At about the 45-minute mark, add the cubed salt pork, chopped bacon, chopped hot dogs and crumbled chorizo.",
    "After about 2 1/2 hours total, add the onion, tomatoes and jalapenos, cover, and cook about 45 minutes more until the beans are tender.",
    "Serve as charro beans, or cool overnight for the next step.",
    "The next day, reheat the beans in a wide pot and add 6 ounces more chorizo.",
    "Add the jalapenos and chipotle peppers and blend with an immersion blender until mostly smooth.",
    "Stir in the Oaxaca and Chihuahua cheese a handful at a time until melted.",
    "Let cool about 10 minutes, then serve with chips."
  ],
  "equipment": [
    "slow cooker",
    "immersion blender"
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Make a big batch of charro beans and chill overnight; this is the restaurant trick for frijoles puercos.",
    "Stir constantly while adding the cheese so it melts into the beans."
  ],
